# media_profiles_vendor.xml is a SYMLINK in stock's vendor image, and
# extract_utils drops symlinks (`find -type l` finds none under our extracted
# vendor/etc), so the target never shipped. Pointing at a non-existent file is
# FATAL, not benign: MediaProfiles only uses its built-in fallback list when the
# property is UNSET; once set it goes straight to createInstanceFromXmlFile(),
# whose CHECK(fopen) is LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL -- which aborted zygote in
# preloadClasses -> CamcorderProfile.<clinit>, i.e. a boot loop caused purely by
# this property port. Repointed at the cliffs profile we actually ship (SM8635
# is "cliffs"; the official peridot device on the same SoC uses cliffs_v0).
