# NFC. /vendor/bin/init.oem.hw.sh derives every ro.vendor.hw.* value from
# /vendor/etc/vhw.xml at boot, but it is unlabelled here so init refuses to exec
# it (stock labels it init_hw_exec):
#   init: Command 'exec_start vendor.oem-hw-sh' ... File /vendor/bin/init.oem.hw.sh
#   (labeled "u:object_r:vendor_file:s0") has incorrect label or no domain transition
# so ro.vendor.hw.nfc comes out EMPTY and nothing ever starts the NFC HAL.
#
# Hardcoding is exact rather than a guess: vhw.xml's arcfox section maps nfc to
# ese_st for every hwid (map=1:ese_st,2:ese_st,3:ese_st,4:ese_st) and for all five
# SKUs, and stock reports ro.vendor.hw.nfc=ese_st.
#
# Deliberately NOT setting ro.vendor.hw.felica: it is true only for radio=JPN,
# and empty already behaves as false for every trigger and for the HAL.
ro.vendor.hw.nfc=ese_st

